# 05-strangler-fig run 2026-09-27T18:45:54Z
== no infra: legacy monolith, new service and routing proxy as three real HTTP servers ==
proxy :53000 (clients only ever call this), legacy :53001, new service :53002
recorded legacy responses as the contract baseline

## 0. Put the facade in front
   concept: clients switch to the proxy once; it forwards everything to legacy, nothing else changes
   routes: (none, everything falls through to legacy)
   GET /users/1    -> legacy-monolith same contract as legacy: true
   GET /orders/1   -> legacy-monolith same contract as legacy: true
   GET /invoices/1 -> legacy-monolith same contract as legacy: true
   legacy handled 3/3 client requests

## 1. Strangle the first capability
   concept: build /orders in the new service, then flip one route; clients see the same contract
   routes: /orders -> new
   GET /users/1    -> legacy-monolith same contract as legacy: true
   GET /orders/1   -> new-service     same contract as legacy: true
   GET /invoices/1 -> legacy-monolith same contract as legacy: true
   legacy handled 2/3 client requests

## 2. Roll back in one call
   concept: if the new service misbehaves, point the route back; no deploy, no client change
   routes: (none, everything falls through to legacy)
   GET /users/1    -> legacy-monolith same contract as legacy: true
   GET /orders/1   -> legacy-monolith same contract as legacy: true
   GET /invoices/1 -> legacy-monolith same contract as legacy: true
   legacy handled 3/3 client requests

## 3. Move more capabilities
   concept: orders again, then invoices: the new system grows around the old one
   routes: /orders -> new, /invoices -> new
   GET /users/1    -> legacy-monolith same contract as legacy: true
   GET /orders/1   -> new-service     same contract as legacy: true
   GET /invoices/1 -> new-service     same contract as legacy: true
   legacy handled 1/3 client requests

## 4. Last route moved, legacy receives nothing
   concept: zero traffic to legacy is the signal it can be switched off
   routes: /orders -> new, /invoices -> new, /users -> new
   GET /users/1    -> new-service     same contract as legacy: true
   GET /orders/1   -> new-service     same contract as legacy: true
   GET /invoices/1 -> new-service     same contract as legacy: true
   legacy handled 0/3 client requests
